  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax-spoorenbergi-2/",
      "html": "<p>Only extremely rarely, this pretty killifish, which grows to a maximum of 7 cm, is offered in the trade. Formerly, Fundulopanchax spoorenbergi was placed in the genus Aphyosemion.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax-spoorenbergi-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species occurs from Nigeria to Cameroon.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax-spoorenbergi-2/",
      "html": "<p>The males of Fundulopanchax spoorenbergi like to quarrel and are always ready to mate. Therefore, numerous hiding places in the aquarium must be provided for inferior males and annoyed females. Even if killifish in general are not well suited for typical community aquariums (they simply get lost there), they can still be kept problem free together with small tetras and barbs of the region.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax-spoorenbergi-2/",
      "html": "<p>Not as short-lived as many killifish: this species lives approximately as long as other popular aquarium fish, like guppies or platies.</p>"
    }
  ],
